# GulaschGo SDLC gate

When working on a `/sdlc` loop or when plan / implement / test / review agents are in play:

- Order is **plan → human gate → implement → test → review**.
- After planning, **stop** until a human explicitly approves the plan.
- Do not implement, test, or review a slice whose plan is not `approved`.
- Keep slices thin and PS1-era low-poly browser-game scoped.
- Write handoffs using `docs/sdlc/templates/` into the active run directory.

## Models

- **Project default** and **orchestrator**: Claude Opus 4.8 — Cursor ID `claude-opus-4-8`.
- **Phase agents** (`plan`, `implement`, `test`, `review`): Claude Sonnet 4.6 — Cursor ID `claude-sonnet-4-6` (pinned in `.cursor/agents/*.md`).
- Do not switch the four agents to `inherit` or another model; do not run the Project/orchestrator on anything other than Opus 4.8 for SDLC work.

Canonical Project doc: Project store `docs/sdlc.md` (when available). Repo overview: `docs/sdlc/README.md`.
